  "findings": [
   {
    "code": "count_mismatch",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The bundle holds 1.46929e+06 where the producer reported 1.47083e+06 (results.txt: All target PSMs with q-value <= 0.01 (pxreprise:DEF-PSM-1PCT v1)). Both numbers are kept; treat the producer's as canonical until the difference is explained."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_stored",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Of 799886 occupancy entries MetaMorpheus wrote, some are not in ptm_stoichiometry: 9403 site not in ptm_sites. 'site not in ptm_sites' means the entry's site has no ptm_sites row to key on; 'not determinable' means a cell's segments could not be assigned to its accessions from the sequences (QuantProject DEF-OCC-ACCESSION), which is never guessed. Absence of a row for these sites is therefore not NA. A 'duplicate' is a second entry for a (site, run) that already has a row: one with identical values loses nothing; one with DIFFERENT values means MetaMorpheus wrote two answers and the first in file order was stored (examples in bundle.json occupancy.differing_duplicates; which one should be stored is QuantProject's to define)."
   },
   {
    "code": "peptide_rows_localization_ambiguous",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "1889 row(s) of AllQuantifiedPeptides.tsv name several full sequences, joined by `|`: a peptide whose modification site the search did not settle (MetaMorpheus #2917). Their 10575 value(s) are not stored, since storing them under one of the sequences would place them on a site the search never decided. The PSMs behind them are in `psms`. E.g. `AAAAM[Common Artifact:Carbamyl on M]AVSEAWPELELAER|[Common Artifact:Carbamyl on X]AAAAMAVSEAWPELELAER`, `AADEDELKEIAFDSSLVFIPAEFRPAPLQN[Common Artifact:Deamidation on N]MLPSLMAPLR|AADEDELKEIAFDSSLVFIPAEFRPAPLQ[Common Artifact:Deamidation on Q]NMLPSLMAPLR`, `AADK[Common Biological:Glutarylation on K]D[Metal:Calcium on D]TC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]FSTEGPNLVTR|AAD[Metal:Calcium on D]K[Common Biological:Glutarylation on K]DTC[Common Fixed:Carbamidomethyl on C]FSTEGPNLVTR`."
   },
   {
    "code": "sdrf_conflicting_rows",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The SDRF's rows for one source name disagree on 34 sample-level cell(s), in 34 sample(s), so those samples have no value there: no sample_characteristics row, and a samples column read from the cell is NULL (organism falls back to the manifest's). No row's value was taken over another's. Disagreeing rows usually mean the SDRF gave several samples one source name, so sample-level questions on these columns cannot be answered until it is curated. characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse103` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_103_20181123103626) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_103_20180626160204); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse104` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_104) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_104); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse105` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_105) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_105); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse107` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_107) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_107); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse108` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_108) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_108); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse109` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_109) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_109); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse111` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_111) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_111); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse112` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_112) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_112); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse113` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_113) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_113); characteristics[extract] of `PXD036532-mouse116` is `NaCl extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_NaCl_116) or `urea/thiourea extract` (1 row(s): 1806_AT_U_116); and 24 more."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 16285 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_decoy_groups",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "210 occupancy entries on decoy protein groups were not stored: MetaMorpheus computes them, and they are FDR machinery, not biology."
   }
